    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Tyler Soderstrom** leads the charge with an elite 76.91 score, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Merrill Kelly (5.31 xERA) and the benefit of hitting second in the order. He is joined at the top of the board by **James Wood** (71.14) and **Mickey Moniak** (69.64). Both outfielders see their projections bolstered by significant park factors (+14%) and advantageous order slots. **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains a mandatory start at 70.68, as his dynamic platoon edge against Roupp provides the highest floor among our corner infielders. While **Austin Riley** carries a strong 65.70 projection, his status is the most precarious due to a 35% rain risk; he remains in the UTIL spot for now, but his outcome is highly weather-dependent.\n\nThe decision to keep **Josh Naylor** (59.86) on the bench was the most difficult call of the morning. While he projects well, his efficiency score fell just short of the starters due to a poor BvP history and a park penalty that suppressed his overall ceiling compared to the likes of **Isaac Paredes** and **Seiya Suzuki**. We are effectively fading the mediocre matchup against Singer to maintain our target efficiency metrics. Conversely, **Corbin Carroll** (59.78) stays in the lineup despite a sub-60 score because his unique ability to impact the SB category\u2014our scarcest asset\u2014outweighs a pure projection-based benching. We will keep a close watch on **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Isaac Paredes**, **James Wood**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Austin Riley** as official lineups drop to confirm their assumed spots, ensuring that the 5x5 production aligns with our daily efficiency mandates.",
